@bobbypage @kannon92 Regarding the `DisruptionTarget` condition this is WAI. The condition is added when the pod is disrupted due to external factors - the eviction manager needs to reclaim memory / disk space. The pod itself does not exceed the limits. 

In the second case from the [comment](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/120182#issuecomment-1693956635) it is the pod itself that exceeds the limits. In that case we considered adding the `ResourceExceeded` condition, but it was tricky to make it fully correct as we intended to reuse the same condition for OOM killing and memory limits. In particular, it is not clear if OOM killed container exceeded its limits, or it was oom killed due to memory pressure. Thus, we left adding the `ResourceExceeded` condition as a potential follow up.

