code:
https://github.com/likakuli/kubernetes/blame/ead7d66ee12656cfb7c633dd42a87f8d9cfaa469/pkg/kubelet/util/manager/cache_based_manager.go#L180-L203

```golang
if data.err != nil || !s.isObjectFresh(data) {
	opts := metav1.GetOptions{}
	if data.object != nil && data.err == nil {
		// This is just a periodic refresh of an object we successfully fetched previously.
		// In this case, server data from apiserver cache to reduce the load on both
		// etcd and apiserver (the cache is eventually consistent).
		util.FromApiserverCache(&opts)
	}

	object, err := s.getObject(namespace, name, opts)
	if err != nil && !apierrors.IsNotFound(err) && data.object == nil && data.err == nil {
		// Couldn't fetch the latest object, but there is no cached data to return.
		// Return the fetch result instead.
		return object, err
	}
	if (err == nil && !isObjectOlder(object, data.object)) || apierrors.IsNotFound(err) {
		// If the fetch succeeded with a newer version of the object, or if the
		// object could not be found in the apiserver, update the cached data to
		// reflect the current status.
		data.object = object
		data.err = err
		data.lastUpdateTime = s.clock.Now()
	}
}
```
The invocation chain is quite lengthy and the reason like blow:
1.  kubelet has a ticker with 1s interval and will try to get pods from queue to sync if there is data in syncCh;
2. the `--sync-frequency` is default set to 1m. pod will be enqueued with a random time between 1m ~ 1.5m by default;
3. there is background reconcicler in `pkg/kubelet/volumemanager/reconciler/reconciler.go` file. it will run every 100ms to try to mountAttachVolumes which could trigger configmap get operation when the volume is not mounted or require remount;
4. data.object will be set to nil each time pod to sync via `AddReference`. pay attention to the comment.
```golang
    // This will trigger fetch on the next Get() operation.
    item.data = nil
``` 
5. when to mount or remount volume, a configmap get request will be triggered and because the data.object is nil, the resourceversion query will not be added which result to the request goes to etcd finally.
6. after volume mounted, the `remountRequired` flag will be set to false in `actualStateOfWorld`;
7. thus when next mountAttachVolumes called but volume has been mounted and not require remount, no need to get configmap from kubelet's cache. therefore there will no http request to apiserver to get configmap;
8. there may be some configmap get operation can be satisfied by cachebasedmanager by directly returned from local cache or get it from apiserver's cache when cache expired because same configmap can be used by many pods and each pod has a goroutine to execute syncPod but only one goroutine to execute mountAttachVolumes.


I think we can always set resourceversion=0 to the query and ignore whether it's the first time to fetch the configmap or just the local cache expired. The implementation of informer is also just to list all specified resources with resourceversion=0 when to start.

